{"id": "EUVD-2026-104583", "enisaUuid": "9911cc20-2016-3f1c-9486-fe20b0edb8a2", "description": "Craft CMS 4.x before 4.18.8 and 5.x before 5.11.0 contains a blocklist bypass in the Twig create() function because its class-name checks are case-sensitive while PHP class resolution is not. Attackers with template-execution rights, such as Control Panel administrators, can instantiate SplFileObject via a lowercase class name to read .env secrets or write a PHP file into the webroot for remote code execution.", "datePublished": "2026-10-19T19:10:54", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T16:09:54", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/craftcms/cms/security/advisories/GHSA-w643-x88w-6wcm", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/craft-cms-before-4.18.8-and-5.11.0-twig-create-blocklist-bypass-leading-to-rce"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-112777", "GHSA-f7pv-pv9r-vg93"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.49, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "52a187e1-331d-37da-adaa-25027d9be6fa", "product": {"name": "CMS", "vendor": {"name": "statamic"}}, "product_version": "5.0.0 <5.11.0"}, {"id": "7027bf62-c607-3b27-a437-560421eb5e11", "product": {"name": "CMS", "vendor": {"name": "statamic"}}, "product_version": "4.0.0 <4.18.8"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9651581b-7e39-3257-aacb-613c9b05be64", "vendor": {"name": "craftcms"}}], "isExploited": false}